fbterm-compat.patch -- xterm sequence compatibility for FbTerm 1.7
==================================================================

Stock FbTerm 1.7 (as packaged by Debian, fbterm 1.7-5) predates
several xterm escape sequences that modern programs emit
unconditionally, without consulting terminfo (fastfetch is one):

  * SGR 90-97 / 100-107      bright foreground/background colours
  * SGR 38;5;<n> / 48;5;<n>  256-colour foreground/background
  * SGR 38;2 / 48;2          truecolor (approximated to the cube)
  * OSC sequences            (OSC 8 hyperlinks, OSC 52, titles...)

Without this patch, SGR 48;5;<n> turns blink on, and an OSC 8
hyperlink ("ESC ] 8 ;; file://... BEL") leaks onto the screen as
garbage text, because FbTerm's parser had no OSC state at all.

The patch teaches FbTerm's VT parser:
  * src/lib/vterm_action.cpp: the SGR codes above, in
    set_display_attr(); FbTerm's CharAttr already stores 8-bit
    colour indices and its renderer already has a 256-colour
    palette (used by its private ESC[1;<n>} sequences), so this
    is purely a parser addition. Legacy SGR 38 behaviour
    (default colour + underline) is kept for the non-extended form.
  * src/lib/vterm_states.cpp + src/lib/vterm.cpp + vterm.h: a real
    OSC state (ESosc). An OSC is consumed until BEL, CAN, SUB or
    ST (ESC \) and dropped, except FbTerm's own palette commands
    (ESC ] P... / ESC ] R), which are handed to the legacy
    ESnonstd state unchanged. ESC \ is also accepted as a string
    terminator in the ESesc state.

Apply AFTER the Debian patch series (build-fbterm-patched.sh does
the full download/patch/build/install cycle):

    patch -p1 < fbterm-compat.patch

Result: /usr/local/bin/fbterm-patched (stock /usr/bin/fbterm is
not touched).

